# Exalo Git ownership

Cursor/AI may inspect and **stage** Git changes when the product owner explicitly asks for staging/checkpoint preparation.

Cursor/AI must **never**:

- `git commit`
- `git push`
- create tags
- amend / rebase / merge
- `reset --hard`
- force push
- rewrite history
- auto-create a checkpoint commit

After staging (when requested), **STOP**. The product owner reviews the staged diff, then commits and pushes manually.

This applies to all Exalo frontend milestones unless the product owner explicitly overrides it in writing.
